[0.1.3]
* Update Cognee 1.6.6 to 1.6.8 (commit 069f3cc, includes 1.6.7). Security items in upstream's notes (1.6.7): raw database connection strings and connection strings carrying Cognee's own credentials are refused by default; server file paths sent over HTTP are refused by default; `ACCEPT_LOCAL_FILE_PATH` now also gates `s3://` inputs; blocked file ingestion answers 403 instead of 415.
* **The graph database engine (Ladybug) moves from 0.19.0 to 0.22.3, and this is a one-way change.** Upstream states that 0.22.3 opens stores written by 0.17.1 to 0.19.0 in place; the first start after updating upgrades the graph storage format (code 43 to 49). A test with the previous image confirmed it: Ladybug 0.19.0 refuses the upgraded store ("Database file version: 49, Current build storage version: 43"), so a rollback to package 0.1.2 cannot open it. Take a Cloudron backup before updating. Upstream makes the move because 0.19.0 could exhaust its database size budget during a long cognify and leave the store unopenable (upstream issue 6679). The baked Ladybug extension image is updated to match (it now carries the v0.22.0 JSON extension that 0.22.3 requests). Ladybug's default maximum database size also rises from 32 GiB to 128 GiB; this is address-space accounting, not disk use.
* Upstream behaviour changes: on the API server, `ALLOW_HTTP_REQUESTS` (ingesting from a web URL) and `ALLOW_DATABASE_INGESTION` are now off unless set, so URL and database-connection ingestion through the API stop working until an operator sets them in the app's environment. This package keeps `ACCEPT_LOCAL_FILE_PATH=true`, which it already set. The `instructor` library is no longer installed with the core package (the default structured-output path does not use it). The LanceDB (0.39) pin is unchanged.
* New upstream features, none switched on by this package: a Slack connector and app, integration sync schedules, and a RabbitMQ embedding worker. Two additive database migrations (integration sync policies and a credentials column) run on the first start. Dependency updates: fastembed 0.9.1 and pydantic 2.13 floors, onnxruntime floor lowered, enola-cli 0.5.1, docling 2.116.

[0.1.2]
* Update Cognee 1.6.5 to 1.6.6 (commit df2b4fa). Security items in upstream's notes: cleanup operations now check delete permission before removing data, and key-management errors are surfaced to the caller instead of being hidden.
* Upstream behaviour changes: conflict review is on by default (a new durable conflict-resolution API is added); fastembed moves from 0.8.0 or older to 0.9.1 or newer, and the package keeps its model cache at /app/models/fastembed; the diskcache dependency is removed; Redis list and context deletes are atomic. The LanceDB (0.39) and Ladybug (0.19.0) pins are unchanged, so the baked Ladybug extension image is unchanged. Upstream's offline benchmark reference results (about 6 MB under `eval_framework`) are left out of the image: the server does not use them. Conflict review runs as a stage of `POST /api/v1/improve`; without an LLM key that stage is skipped and add, cognify and search are unaffected. On the first start after the update LanceDB trims its table version history (rows and the graph are unchanged), so the data directory shrinks sharply.

[0.1.1]
* Base image cloudron/base 6.0.0 to 6.0.1: Ubuntu security updates, including the removal of the compromised eMudhra emSign ECC Root CA - G3 from the trusted certificates.
* Update Cognee 1.6.2 to 1.6.5 (commit 37f788b). Security items in upstream's notes: public sign-up no longer accepts a parent account (1.6.3), extraction reasons are removed from logs (1.6.3), and the Google Calendar connector was hardened (1.6.5). Self-registration is closed in this package.
* Upstream behaviour changes: the `temporal_cognify` option is removed; LanceDB's automatic background pruning is removed (this package now prunes it daily, see below); the DLT dependency is pinned below 1.31; agents can no longer create other agents.
* The bundled Node.js for the web interface moves from 22 (unversioned tag) to 22.23.4, the 2026-10-20 security release.
* New daily job (03:30, the platform's scheduler) that compacts LanceDB and removes versions older than `COGNEE_LANCEDB_RETENTION_DAYS` (default 7), because upstream no longer prunes and the file count in the backed-up data directory would otherwise grow without bound. Set the variable in the app's environment to change the retention.

[0.1.0]
* First release: Cognee 1.6.2 (upstream release v1.6.2, commit ba3631f), built on cloudron/base 6.0.0.
* API and web interface behind one address; PostgreSQL from the platform, graph and vector stores as files
  in the data directory.
* Sign-in by email and password. Self-registration is closed and telemetry is off. The three signing
  secrets and the administrator password are generated once and kept in the data directory.
* The local extraction and embedding models download on first use into a persistent directory that is left
  out of backups. A language model is optional and can be any OpenAI-compatible endpoint; with one, and an
  embedding endpoint, neither local model is fetched.
* `set-admin-email.sh` renames the administrator safely.
